{
    "background_story": "Angie was a free-spirited travel writer who had always been fascinated by the rich history and culture of Croatia. Born to Croatian parents in the United States, she felt a deep connection to her ancestral homeland. After college, Angie embarked on a journey to explore the Dalmatian coast, immersing herself in the local customs and traditions. She spent countless hours learning the language, sampling the delicious seafood, and dancing to the rhythms of traditional Croatian folk music. As she wandered through the ancient streets of Dubrovnik and Split, Angie felt an overwhelming sense of belonging. She eventually settled in a quaint village on the island of Hvar, where she wrote a bestselling novel about her experiences. Angie's love for Croatia and its people inspired her to become an ambassador for Croatian culture, sharing its beauty with the world through her writing.",
